  "question": {
    "text": "The number of orbitals with <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></math> is ________. (Round off to the Nearest Integer)."
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "3",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>For,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#8467;</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>If <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#8467;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#8467;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced open=\"{\" close=\"}\"><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#8467;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced open=\"{\" close=\"}\"><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#8467;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced open=\"{\" close=\"}\"><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#8467;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced open=\"{\" close=\"}\"><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>5</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">f</mi></math>&nbsp;and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></math> subshell contain one-one orbital having <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mi>&#8467;</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></math></p>"
